---
import BaseLayout from "../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";

const title = "Signalbriar privacy policy | Patrik Dóczy";
const description =
  "How the Signalbriar mobile game uses local save data, Google advertising, optional gameplay analytics, remote configuration, and app-store purchases.";
---

<BaseLayout {title} {description} pathname="/privacy/signalbriar/">
  <header class="page-hero">
    <div class="shell">
      <nav class="breadcrumbs" aria-label="Breadcrumb">
        <a href="/">Home</a><span aria-hidden="true">/</span><a href="/privacy/"
          >Privacy</a
        ><span aria-hidden="true">/</span><span aria-current="page"
          >Signalbriar</span
        >
      </nav>
      <p class="eyebrow">Mobile game privacy policy</p>
      <h1>Signalbriar privacy</h1>
      <p class="lede">
        Local progression, optional gameplay analytics, and clear controls for
        advertising privacy.
      </p>
      <p class="updated">Last updated: 5 September 2026</p>
    </div>
  </header>

  <section class="section">
    <div class="shell content-grid">
      <aside>
        <p class="eyebrow">Signalbriar</p>
        <p><a href="/privacy/">Website privacy</a></p>
        <p>
          <a href="mailto:doczy.patrik410@gmail.com">Privacy contact</a>
        </p>
      </aside>
      <div class="prose">
        <div class="note">
          <p>
            This policy covers the Signalbriar mobile game for Android and iOS.
            Signalbriar is a general-audience game and is not directed to
            children.
          </p>
        </div>

        <h2>Who is responsible for the data</h2>
        <p>
          Patrik Dóczy is the developer and data controller for Signalbriar.
          Privacy questions and requests can be sent to{" "}
          <a href="mailto:doczy.patrik410@gmail.com"
            >doczy.patrik410@gmail.com</a
          >.
        </p>

        <h2>Information stored on your device</h2>
        <p>
          Signalbriar stores gameplay progress, earned and equipped appearance
          items, settings, tutorial state, advertising-scheduler counters, and
          an entitlement cache for the Premium upgrade on your device. This
          information is used to operate the game and preserve your choices.
        </p>
        <p>
          Local game data remains until you reset it through a supported game
          control, clear the app’s storage, or uninstall the app. Store-owned
          purchase records are controlled separately by Apple or Google and can
          be used to restore Premium.
        </p>

        <h2>Advertising</h2>
        <p>
          The iOS 1.0 release requests nonpersonalised ads and disables Google’s
          publisher first-party identifier used for ad personalisation. Ads are
          not selected using your cross-app browsing or app-use history.
          Nonpersonalised ads may still process the information below for
          delivery, frequency limits, measurement, security, and fraud
          prevention. Google’s applicable consent and opt-out choices continue
          to apply. Android production advertising is not enabled in this
          release work.
        </p>
        <p>
          The free mobile version uses Google AdMob to request and display
          interstitial advertisements between eligible runs. Google’s mobile
          advertising software may collect or share an IP address, approximate
          location inferred from that address, app and advertisement
          interactions, diagnostic information, and device or account
          identifiers for advertising, measurement, security, and fraud
          prevention. The exact treatment depends on your region, device
          settings, and privacy choices.
        </p>
        <p>
          Where required, Google’s consent form offers choices for personalised
          advertising and data processing before an advertisement is requested.
          Eligible users can revisit those choices through the game’s <strong
            >Privacy Options</strong
          > control. Signalbriar honours applicable opt-out signals and uses the most
          restrictive available advertising treatment.
        </p>
        <p>
          Signalbriar does not request Apple’s App Tracking Transparency
          permission and does not use Apple’s Identifier for Advertisers. It
          does not request precise location, contacts, microphone, camera, or
          photo-library access for advertising. Buying or restoring Premium
          disables Signalbriar’s interstitial advertising requests.
        </p>
        <p>
          Learn more in{" "}
          <a href="https://policies.google.com/privacy"
            >Google’s privacy policy</a
          >{" "}and on{" "}
          <a href="https://policies.google.com/technologies/partner-sites"
            >Google’s information page for partner apps and sites</a
          >.
        </p>

        <h2>Optional gameplay analytics</h2>
        <p>
          Gameplay analytics are disabled by default. After the first Signal
          Draft tutorial, Signalbriar may ask for separate permission to send
          bounded gameplay and monetisation events to GameAnalytics. Declining
          or dismissing the request does not restrict gameplay, and the choice
          can be changed later in Settings.
        </p>
        <p>
          If enabled, the data can include a pseudonymous, randomly generated
          analytics identifier and Apple device-vendor identifier; app version
          and platform; run mode and sector; run start and settlement; clear or
          defeat result; active gameplay duration; kill and draft counts;
          advertising availability and outcomes; Signalkeeper Pack views; and
          purchase, restoration, or entitlement outcomes. For a newly completed
          Premium purchase, the event may also include the actual purchase
          amount and three-letter currency supplied by the app store. These
          events are used to understand game balance, reliability, advertising
          frequency, and Premium conversion.
        </p>
        <p>
          Signalbriar does not send names, email addresses, account identifiers,
          precise location, free-form text, save paths, run seeds, receipts,
          signed purchase payloads, purchase tokens, transaction or order
          identifiers, store-account identifiers, or payment-card details to
          GameAnalytics. Withdrawing analytics permission stops future gameplay
          event submission; it does not automatically erase events already
          processed.
        </p>

        <h2>Remote configuration</h2>
        <p>
          Signalbriar may contact GameAnalytics to obtain bounded operational
          settings, such as whether monetisation is enabled and the minimum time
          between advertisements, even when you have not opted in to
          gameplay-event submission. This Remote Config request can expose basic
          technical request data that an online service normally receives, such
          as an IP address, platform, app and SDK version, and network-request
          metadata. Declining, dismissing, or withdrawing gameplay analytics
          keeps gameplay-event submission off; it does not disable Remote
          Config. If a valid setting is unavailable, the game uses its last
          valid settings or compiled defaults.
        </p>
        <p>
          GameAnalytics processes analytics on Patrik’s behalf. Its current data
          schedule retains raw and annotated data for one month, player
          warehouse data for one year, and player lookup data for up to 18
          months. See the{" "}
          <a href="https://www.gameanalytics.com/trust/privacy-faq"
            >GameAnalytics developer policy</a
          >{" "}and{" "}
          <a
            href="https://docs.gameanalytics.com/event-tracking-and-integrations/data-retention-and-limits/data-retention-practices/"
            >data-retention documentation</a
          >.
        </p>

        <h2>Premium purchases</h2>
        <p>
          Premium purchases and restorations are processed by the Apple App
          Store or Google Play. Signalbriar receives only the transaction or
          entitlement information needed to grant and restore Premium; Patrik
          does not receive your payment-card details. The store provider’s
          privacy policy governs its payment and account processing.
        </p>

        <h2>Children</h2>
        <p>
          Signalbriar is not designed for or directed to children. Patrik does
          not knowingly collect personal information from children. A player who
          is below the age at which they can provide valid consent should not
          enable optional gameplay analytics without permission from a parent or
          guardian where required by law. If you believe a child has provided
          personal information through Signalbriar, contact Patrik using the
          address above.
        </p>

        <h2>Your choices and rights</h2>
        <p>
          You can disable gameplay analytics in Settings, revisit applicable
          advertising choices through <strong>Privacy Options</strong>, buy or
          restore Premium to remove interstitial advertisements, and delete
          local game data using device or supported in-game controls.
        </p>
        <p>
          Depending on where you live, you may have rights to access, correct,
          delete, restrict, or object to processing of personal information, to
          withdraw consent, or to receive a portable copy. Some United States
          laws may describe personalised advertising as a “sale” or “sharing”;
          eligible users can submit the provided opt-out choice without being
          denied the game’s normal functionality.
        </p>
        <p>
          Send a request to{" "}
          <a href="mailto:doczy.patrik410@gmail.com"
            >doczy.patrik410@gmail.com</a
          >. Because Signalbriar has no player accounts and uses pseudonymous
          identifiers, Patrik may need information available in the app’s
          Settings screen to locate relevant analytics data. You may also
          complain to your local data-protection authority.
        </p>

        <h2>International processing and security</h2>
        <p>
          Google, GameAnalytics, Apple, and their service providers may process
          information in countries other than yours, using the safeguards
          described in their policies and applicable agreements. Signalbriar and
          its providers use reasonable technical and organisational safeguards,
          but no storage or transmission system can be guaranteed completely
          secure.
        </p>

        <h2>Policy changes</h2>
        <p>
          This policy will be updated before Signalbriar materially changes its
          data collection, providers, purposes, or player controls. The date at
          the top identifies the current version.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>
